  "mechaber/part-001.txt": {
    "1:main": "The law of a barrel that broke. And in it 5 seifim: A barrel that broke — one may save from it food for three meals, even in many vessels; for if in one vessel, even if it holds one hundred meals — one may save; and one may say to others: come and save for yourselves; provided that he does not sponge — that is, he should not place the sponge in the place of the wine to return and drip it — a decree lest he come to squeeze; and even if it has a handle such that there is no concern of squeezing — forbidden, that he should not do as he does on a weekday; and he should not dab with oil to insert his hand and wipe it on the lip of the vessel. {Rama: And some say that specifically a barrel that broke that he is panicked — if he may save we are concerned lest he repair it; but if it cracked and drips drop by drop such that he is not so panicked — permitted to save in vessels to collect and to combine [Hagahot Mordechai and Tosafos chapter Kol Kitvei and Hagahot Maimoni chapter 24]; and some say that all this speaks only of saving from courtyard to courtyard, but to another house that made eruv with him — one may save in every manner, as explained above regarding fire (Piskei Maharai 196).}",
    "2:main": "If it broke on the top of his roof — he brings a vessel and places it beneath it; provided that he does not bring another vessel and collect what splashes in the air after it descended from the roof, and he should not bring another vessel and attach it to the top of the roof; but if he saves in one vessel — he may save even by collecting in the air or by attaching.",
    "3:main": "If guests happened to come to him — he brings one vessel and collects, one vessel and combines; and he should not collect and combine and afterward invite his guests; and he should not employ a stratagem to invite guests who do not need to eat. {Rama: However, if he transgressed and did so — that he collected and afterward invited guests — it is permitted (Rambam and Maggid Mishneh chapter 22).}",
    "4:main": "If wine drips from a vat of grapes that have not yet been trodden — that drip that is found is not fit, for the liquids that flowed are forbidden; and he is not permitted to place a vessel beneath it because he nullifies it from its primary use. How should he act? He places his bed or table there, and then that drip is before him like a chamber pot; and he may place a vessel there to receive the drip so that he does not make mud there; and when the vessel fills — he should not pour it into another vessel lest he nullify it from its primary use, but rather he pours it back into the vat from which the liquid flowed, for it is nullified from its primary use by the liquids in it on account of liquids that flowed.",
    "5:main": "If fruits scattered for him in the courtyard — one here and one there — he gathers little by little and eats, and he should not place them into the basket or into the tub; but if they fell in one place — he may place them even into the basket; unless they fell into pebbles and dust in the courtyard — then he gathers one by one and eats, and he should not place them into the basket or into the tub (and see above siman 319):"
  },
